age[\"Sensor_Name\"].unique())\n","        vars_seen.update(df_page[\"Variable\"].unique())\n","        page_min, page_max = df_page[\"Timestamp\"].min(), df_page[\"Timestamp\"].max()\n","        ts_min = page_min if ts_min is None else min(ts_min, page_min)\n","        ts_max = page_max if ts_max is None else max(ts_max, page_max)\n","\n","        print(f\"Page {page:>3}: {len(df_page):>4} rows  (cumulative: {total_rows:>7,})\")\n","\n","        if len(df_page) < PAGE_SIZE:\n","            print(\"Last page reached.\")\n","            break\n","\n","        offset += PAGE_SIZE\n","        page   += 1\n","        del df_page, table        # free memory immediately\n","        time.sleep(PAUSE)\n","\n","    if writer is not None:\n","        writer.close()\n","\n","    print(f\"\\nWrote          : {OUT_PATH}\")\n","    print(f\"Total rows     : {total_rows:,}\")\n","    print(f\"Sensors        : {len(sensors_seen)}\")\n","    print(f\"Variables      : {sorted(vars_seen)}\")\n","    print(f\"Date range     : {ts_min} → {ts_max}\")\n","    print(\"\\nLoad later with: df_30d = pd.read_parquet('data_export/uo_30d_all_themes.parquet')\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6596cc47","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.050658,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.722462","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.671804","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 9b. Full Archive Acquisition — Population Data (June 2013 → Present)\n","\n","### Why we fetch the **complete** archive instead of a sample\n","\n","> *\"Calculating the true population mean ($\\mu$) is often practically impossible because it requires data from every member of a large or infinite group, making a census impractical. Instead, researchers use the sample mean ($\\bar{x}$) to estimate the population mean, acknowledging that this is an estimation rather than an exact, known value.\"*\n","\n","This is the standard position taken in two foundational statistics textbooks used in this thesis:\n","\n","- **Lind, Marchal & Wathen (2021)**, *Statistical Techniques in Business and Economics*, 17e\n","  - **Ch 3** (eq 3-1) defines $\\mu = \\dfrac{\\sum x}{N}$ and notes that obtaining all $N$ values is rarely feasible.\n","  - **Ch 8 §8-2 (\"Sampling Error\")** explains *\"since the sample is a part or portion of the population, it is unlikely that the sample mean would be exactly equal to the population mean … This difference is called sampling error.\"*\n","\n","- **Walpole, Myers, Myers & Ye (2017)**, *Probability and Statistics for Engineers and Scientists*, 9e\n","  - **Ch 1, Definition 1.1** introduces the sample mean $\\bar{x}$ as the working estimator whenever the full population is inaccessible.\n","  - **Ch 9** develops one- and two-sample estimation precisely because $\\mu$ is normally unknown.\n","\n","### What makes the Urban Observatory exceptional\n","\n","The Newcastle Urban Observatory is the rare empirical setting where this constraint **does not apply**:\n","\n","| Property | Value |\n","|---|---|\n","| Data scope | Full IoT sensor population for the network |\n","| Archive | Continuous from **18 June 2013 → today** (13+ years) |\n","| Access | Open REST API v2, no authentication |\n","| Coverage | All 15 themes, 112 variable types, 2 128 sensors, 29 brokers |\n","| Cost of a \"census\" | Zero — equivalent to fetching the entire archive |\n","\n","By downloading every reading from 2013 to the present, we obtain $N$ itself, not a sample of it. The mean we compute **is** $\\mu$; the variance **is** $\\sigma^2$. Sampling error (Lind §8-2) **vanishes** for sensor-reading statistics. Confidence intervals on the data are no longer needed — only on the LLM accuracy proportions in §19, where the question pool is conceptually infinite.\n","\n","### Implementation strategy\n","\n","The cell below downloads the archive in **quarterly chunks** across all themes. Each chunk is saved as Parquet, so re-running with `resume=True` skips already-downloaded windows. After completion the function prints exact population parameters $(N, \\mu, \\sigma)$ per variable.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":19,"id":"37a45231","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.821363Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.821009Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.842436Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.841349Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.072575,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.84449","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.771915","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["fetch_full_archive() defined.\n","Quarterly chunks to download: 53 (≈ 1 min at 1.5 s/chunk)\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImports=false, reportUnnecessaryIsInstance=false, reportPrivateImportUsage=false, reportMissingParameterType=false, reportUnusedImport=false, reportArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeArgument=false, reportUndefinedVariable=false, reportGeneralTypeIssues=false, reportOptionalMemberAccess=false, reportOptionalSubscript=false, reportOptionalIterable=false, reportOptionalCall=false, reportReturnType=false, reportAssignmentType=false, reportOptionalOperand=false, reportUnnecessaryComparison=false, reportUnusedFunction=false, reportUnusedVariable=false, reportUnboundVariable=false, reportUnknownLambdaType=false, reportUnusedClass=false\n","import os, time as _time_mod\n","from datetime import datetime, timezone\n","from typing import Optional\n","\n","ARCHIVE_START = datetime(2013, 6, 18, tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n","ARCHIVE_END   = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n","ARCHIVE_DIR   = \"data_export/archive\"\n","os.makedirs(ARCHIVE_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","def _advance_months(dt: datetime, months: int) -> datetime:\n","    \"\"\"Advance a datetime by a number of calendar months.\"\"\"\n","    m = dt.month - 1 + months\n","    return dt.replace(year=dt.year + m // 12, month=m % 12 + 1, day=1)\n","\n","def fetch_full_archive(\n","    variables: Optional[list[str]] = None,\n","    bbox: Optional[list[float]] = None,\n","    chunk_months: int = 3,\n","    page_size: int = 1000,\n","    save_dir: str = ARCHIVE_DIR,\n","    pause: float = 1.5,\n","    resume: bool = True\n",") -> pd.DataFrame:\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Fetch the complete Urban Observatory archive from June 2013 to present.\n","\n","    Downloads in quarterly chunks across all themes. Each chunk is saved as\n","    Parquet — re-running with resume=True skips already-downloaded chunks.\n","    Pass bbox=None to fetch the entire Urban Observatory (all sensors).\n","    \"\"\"\n","    if variables is None:\n","        variables = ALL_VARIABLES\n","    # bbox=None → no geographic filter → ALL sensors in the observatory\n","\n","    os.makedirs(save_dir, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","    windows: list[tuple[datetime, datetime]] = []\n","    cur = ARCHIVE_START\n","    while cur < ARCHIVE_END:\n","        nxt = _advance_months(cur, chunk_months)\n","        windows.append((cur, min(nxt, ARCHIVE_END)))\n","        cur = nxt\n","\n","    bbox_label = f\"{bbox}\" if bbox else \"ALL (no bbox filter)\"\n","    print(f\"Archive span  : {ARCHIVE_START.date()} → {ARCHIVE_END.date()}\")\n","    print(f\"Geographic scope : {bbox_label}\")\n","    print(f\"Time chunks   : {len(windows)} × {chunk_months}-month windows\")\n","    print(f\"Variables     : {len(variables)} across {len(ALL_THEME_VARIABLES)} themes\")\n","    print(f\"Saving to     : {save_dir}/\")\n","    print()\n","\n","    all_frames: list[pd.DataFrame] = []\n","    for i, (start, end) in enumerate(windows):\n","        tag  = start.strftime('%Y%m')\n","        path = os.path.join(save_dir, f\"chunk_{tag}.parquet\")\n","\n","        if resume and os.path.exists(path):\n","            df_c = pd.read_parquet(path)\n","            all_frames.append(df_c)\n","            print(f\"  [{i+1:03d}/{len(windows)}] {start.date()} → {end.date()}: \"\n","                  f\"cache ({len(df_c):,} rows)\")\n","            continue\n","\n","        print(f\"  [{i+1:03d}/{len(windows)}] {start.date()} → {end.date()}: fetching...\",\n","              end=\"\", flush=True)\n","        df_c = fetch_paginated(\n","            variables=variables,\n","            start=start,\n","            end=end,\n","            bbox=bbox,          # None = no filter = all sensors\n","            page_size=page_size,\n","            max_pages=500,\n","            pause=pause,\n","        )\n","\n","        if not df_c.empty:\n","            df_c.to_parquet(path, index=False)\n","            all_frames.append(df_c)\n","            print(f\" {len(df_c):,} rows → saved\")\n","        else:\n","            print(\" no data\")\n","\n","        _time_mod.sleep(pause)\n","\n","    if not all_frames:\n","        print(\"\\nNo data retrieved.\")\n","        return pd.DataFrame()\n","\n","    df_full = pd.concat(all_frames, ignore_index=True)\n","    df_full[\"Timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(df_full[\"Timestamp\"], utc=True)\n","    df_full[\"Value\"]     = pd.to_numeric(df_full[\"Value\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n","    df_full = (df_full\n","               .drop_duplicates(subset=[\"Sensor_Name\", \"Variable\", \"Timestamp\"])\n","               .sort_values([\"Sensor_Name\", \"Variable\", \"Timestamp\"])\n","               .reset_index(drop=True))\n","\n","    span_days = (df_full[\"Timestamp\"].max() - df_full[\"Timestamp\"].min()).days\n","    print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n","    print(f\"Full archive assembled (population dataset):\")\n","    print(f\"  Total rows   : {len(df_full):,}\")\n","    print(f\"  Sensors      : {df_full['Sensor_Name'].nunique()}\")\n","    print(f\"  Variables    : {df_full['Variable'].nunique()} — \"\n","          f\"{sorted(df_full['Variable'].unique().tolist())}\")\n","    print(f\"  Date range   : {df_full['Timestamp'].min()} → {df_full['Timestamp'].max()}\")\n","    print(f\"  Span         : {span_days:,} days ({span_days/365.25:.1f} years)\")\n","    print(f\"{'='*60}\")\n","\n","    print(\"\\nPopulation parameters per variable (μ = true mean, no CI needed):\")\n","    for var, grp in df_full.groupby(\"Variable\"):\n","        vals  = grp[\"Value\"].dropna()\n","        mu    = vals.mean()\n","        sigma = vals.std(ddof=0)\n","        print(f\"  {var:30s}: N={len(vals):>9,}  μ={mu:>9.3f}  σ={sigma:>8.3f}\")\n","    print()\n","    return df_full\n","\n","# ── Count quarterly chunks (no download) ─────────────────────────────────────\n","_cur, _n = ARCHIVE_START, 0\n","while _cur < ARCHIVE_END:\n","    _cur = _advance_months(_cur, 3)\n","    _n += 1\n","\n","print(\"fetch_full_archive() defined.\")\n","print(f\"Quarterly chunks to download: {_n} (≈ {_n * 1.5 / 60:.0f} min at 1.5 s/chunk)\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":20,"id":"59c57738","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.940587Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.940091Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.950347Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.949382Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.060214,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.952394","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:42.89218","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Using bulk archive (no API download): 736 files, 3,526,526,311 rows.\n","  path  : /kaggle/input/datasets/wganme/urban-observatory\n","  query : ARCHIVE_DATASET.to_table(filter=..., columns=...)\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImports=false, reportUnnecessaryIsInstance=false, reportPrivateImportUsage=false, reportMissingParameterType=false, reportUnusedImport=false, reportArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeArgument=false, reportUndefinedVariable=false, reportGeneralTypeIssues=false, reportOptionalMemberAccess=false, reportOptionalSubscript=false, reportOptionalIterable=false, reportOptionalCall=false, reportReturnType=false, reportAssignmentType=false, reportOptionalOperand=false, reportUnnecessaryComparison=false, reportUnusedFunction=false, reportUnusedVariable=false, reportUnboundVariable=false, reportUnknownLambdaType=false, reportUnusedClass=false\n","# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","# Full archive acquisition policy\n","# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# We DO NOT re-download anything that already exists in the bulk Parquet\n","# archive (ARCHIVE_BULK). The bulk archive is the authoritative source.\n","#\n","# Behaviour:\n","#   * If ARCHIVE_BULK_AVAILABLE  → skip the API download entirely; use\n","#     ARCHIVE_DATASET in downstream cells.\n","#   * Else if RUN_FULL_ARCHIVE   → fall back to the API paginated downloader\n","#     (slow; only for the case where the bulk archive is missing).\n","#   * Else                       → skip and continue.\n","# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","RUN_FULL_ARCHIVE = False  # API fallback only; ignored if ARCHIVE_BULK is present\n","\n","if ARCHIVE_BULK_AVAILABLE:\n","    print(\n","        f\"Using bulk archive (no API download): \"\n","        f\"{len(ARCHIVE_FILES):,} files, {ARCHIVE_TOTAL_ROWS:,} rows.\\n\"\n","        f\"  path  : {ARCHIVE_BULK}\\n\"\n","        f\"  query : ARCHIVE_DATASET.to_table(filter=..., columns=...)\"\n","    )\n","elif not RUN_FULL_ARCHIVE:\n","    print(\n","        \"ARCHIVE_BULK not found and RUN_FULL_ARCHIVE=False -> skipping.\\n\"\n","        \"Set RUN_FULL_ARCHIVE=True to fetch from the API instead.\"\n","    )\n","else:\n","    df_full = fetch_full_archive(\n","        variables=ALL_VARIABLES,\n","        bbox=None,            # None = entire Urban Observatory, no geographic filter\n","        chunk_months=3,\n","        page_size=1000,\n","        resume=True,          # skips chunks already saved to disk\n","    )\n","\n","    # Load into SQLite (replaces the sample data)\n","    import sqlite3 as _fb_sqlite3\n","    _fb_db_path = str(Path(WORK_ROOT) / \"data_export\" / \"urban_observatory.db\")\n","    _fb_conn = _fb_sqlite3.connect(_fb_db_path)\n","    df_full.rename(columns={\"Sensor_Name\": \"sensor_name\", \"Variable\": \"variable\",\n","                             \"Value\": \"value\", \"Timestamp\": \"timestamp\",\n","                             \"Flagged\": \"flagged\"}, inplace=True)\n","    df_full[[\"sensor_name\", \"variable\", \"value\", \"timestamp\", \"flagged\"]].to_sql(\n","        \"readings\", _fb_conn, if_exists=\"replace\", index=False)\n","    _fb_conn.commit()\n","    _fb_conn.close()\n","    print(f\"Full population loaded into SQLite via API fallback: {_fb_db_path}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":21,"id":"7653c5bb","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.053037Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.05257Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.066085Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.064934Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.06748,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.068079","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.000599","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["topup_archive() ready. Call topup_archive(run=False) to inspect the gap.\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImports=false, reportUnnecessaryIsInstance=false, reportPrivateImportUsage=false, reportMissingParameterType=false, reportUnusedImport=false, reportArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeArgument=false, reportUndefinedVariable=false, reportGeneralTypeIssues=false, reportOptionalMemberAccess=false, reportOptionalSubscript=false, reportOptionalIterable=false, reportOptionalCall=false, reportReturnType=false, reportAssignmentType=false, reportOptionalOperand=false, reportUnnecessaryComparison=false, reportUnusedFunction=false, reportUnusedVariable=false, reportUnboundVariable=false, reportUnknownLambdaType=false, reportUnusedClass=false\n","# === Incremental top-up: fetch ONLY the gap (archive_max_ts → now) ===\n","# Uses Parquet column statistics (footer metadata) — never loads any data\n","# into RAM. Memory cost is O(n_files) ≈ tens of MB, NOT O(n_rows).\n","\n","from datetime import datetime, timezone\n","\n","TOPUP_PATH = DATA_EXPORT / \"archive_topup.parquet\"\n","\n","\n","def archive_max_timestamp() -> datetime | None:\n","    \"\"\"Return the latest timestamp in the bulk archive, read from Parquet\n","    footer statistics. Does not load any row data.\"\"\"\n","    if not ARCHIVE_BULK_AVAILABLE or not ARCHIVE_FILES:\n","        return None\n","    best: datetime | None = None\n","    for p in ARCHIVE_FILES:\n","        try:\n","            pf = pq.ParquetFile(p)\n","            md = pf.metadata\n","            names = pf.schema_arrow.names\n","            if \"timestamp\" not in names:\n","                continue\n","            col_idx = names.index(\"timestamp\")\n","            for rg in range(md.num_row_groups):\n","                stats = md.row_group(rg).column(col_idx).statistics\n","                if stats is None or stats.max is None:\n","                    continue\n","                v = stats.max\n","                if isinstance(v, datetime):\n","                    if v.tzinfo is None:\n","                        v = v.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n","                    if best is None or v > best:\n","                        best = v\n","        except Exception:\n","            continue\n","    return best\n","\n","\n","def topup_archive(run: bool = False) -> None:\n","    \"\"\"Fetch only the API window (archive_max_ts → now) for ALL_VARIABLES.\"\"\"\n","    if not ARCHIVE_BULK_AVAILABLE:\n","        print(\"ARCHIVE_BULK missing -> nothing to top up.\")\n","        return\n","    max_ts = archive_max_timestamp()\n","    if max_ts is None:\n","        print(\"Could not determine archive max timestamp; aborting top-up.\")\n","        return\n","    now = datetime.now(tz=timezone.utc)\n","    gap_hours = (now - max_ts).total_seconds() / 3600\n","    print(f\"Archive max timestamp : {max_ts.isoformat()}\")\n","    print(f\"Now (UTC)             : {now.isoformat()}\")\n","    print(f\"Gap                   : {gap_hours:,.1f} hours\")\n","    if gap_hours < 1:\n","        print(\"Gap < 1 h -> nothing to fetch.\")\n","        return\n","    if not run:\n","        print(\"\\nSet `topup_archive(run=True)` to actually fetch the gap window.\")\n","        return\n","    if \"fetch_paginated\" not in globals():\n","        print(\"fetch_paginated() is not defined yet; run the API fetch cells first.\")\n","        return\n","    df_gap = fetch_paginated(  # type: ignore[name-defined]\n","        variables=ALL_VARIABLES,  # type: ignore[name-defined]\n","        start=max_ts,\n","        end=now,\n","        bbox=None,\n","        page_size=1000,\n","        max_pages=10_000,\n","        pause=1.0,\n","    )\n","    if df_gap.empty:\n","        print(\"API returned 0 rows for the gap window.\")\n","        return\n","    df_gap.to_parquet(TOPUP_PATH, index=False, compression=\"snappy\")\n","    print(f\"Top-up saved: {TOPUP_PATH} ({len(df_gap):,} rows)\")\n","\n","\n","# Defer auto-run: opening the notebook should NOT trigger any heavy work.\n","# Call topup_archive(run=False) for a status report,\n","# then topup_archive(run=True) to actually fetch the missing gap.\n","print(\"topup_archive() ready. Call topup_archive(run=False) to inspect the gap.\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"53791eaa","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.046293,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.164017","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.117724","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 10. Export Cleaned Results for Reuse\n","\n","Save final datasets to CSV and Parquet for downstream thesis notebooks."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":22,"id":"c6d49665","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.261748Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.26142Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-30T04:34:44.466229Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-30T04:34:44.465082Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.256152,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:44.468413","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:43.212261","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Saved sensors_newcastle.csv (1412 rows)\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Saved aq_24h.csv and .parquet (71814 rows)\n","\n","Exported files: ['all_experiment_results.csv', 'notebook_output.log', 'rag_experiment_results.csv', 'aq_24h.csv', 'sensors_newcastle.csv', 'aq_24h.parquet', 'archive']\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImp