ight_Above_Sea_Level, Broker_Name, Raw_ID | One row per physical device |\n","| `variables` | Name, Units, Upper_Flag, Lower_Flag, Theme | One row per measurement type |\n","| `readings` | Sensor_Name, Variable, Value, Timestamp, Flagged | Fact table: sensor × variable × timestamp |\n","\n","This schema is the basis for the 5-tier SQL complexity taxonomy in **Chapter 3**\n","and the RAG schema-exposure experiments in **Chapter 4**."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8c16dac7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.048742,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:54.318869","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:54.270127","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","\n","# Part II — NL-to-SQL Experiment Pipeline (Chapters 3–4)\n","\n","The sections below implement the full experiment infrastructure:\n","\n","| Section | Purpose | Thesis Chapter |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| 11. SQLite Database | Populate 3-table schema from API exports | Ch 3, 4 |\n","| 12. DDL & Prompt Templates | Schema DDL used in LLM prompts | Ch 3, 4 |\n","| 13. Benchmark Questions (T1–T5) | 50 NL→SQL pairs with ground-truth | Ch 3 |\n","| 14. LLM Inference Setup | Local + cloud model configuration | Ch 3, 4 |\n","| 15. NL-to-SQL Evaluation Pipeline | Run benchmark, compute execution accuracy | Ch 3 |\n","| 16. Pre-Execution Anomaly Detector | Rule-based SQL safety checker | Ch 3 |\n","| 17. RAG Pipeline | Embed schema chunks, retrieve per query | Ch 4 |\n","| 18. Schema Exposure (ρ_exposure) | Token counting & exposure metric | Ch 4 |\n","| 19. Statistical Analysis | Wilson CI, Wilcoxon, Fisher, Cohen's h | Ch 3, 4 |\n","| 20. LaTeX Table Generation | Auto-generate thesis tables from results | Ch 3, 4 |"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6c248d43","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.050705,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:54.420507","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:54.369802","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 11. Build SQLite Database from API Data\n","\n","Create the 3-table relational schema (`sensors`, `variables`, `readings`) in SQLite,\n","populated from the data already fetched via uo-pyfetch. This database is the execution\n","target for all NL-to-SQL experiments in Chapters 3 and 4."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":26,"id":"c343d382","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-30T04:34:54.527452Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-30T04:34:54.526833Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-30T04:34:55.720219Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-30T04:34:55.719054Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.247183,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:55.722831","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:54.475648","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["sensors table: 1412 rows  (cols: ['raw_id', 'broker_name', 'sensor_height', 'sensor_name', 'centroid_lon', 'location_wkt', 'ground_height', 'centroid_lat'])\n","variables table: 114 rows\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["readings table: 72,718 rows\n","  sensors: 1412 rows\n","  variables: 114 rows\n","  readings: 72718 rows\n","\n","Database saved to: /kaggle/working/data_export/urban_observatory.db\n","Size: 11628.0 KB\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImports=false, reportUnnecessaryIsInstance=false, reportPrivateImportUsage=false, reportMissingParameterType=false, reportUnusedImport=false, reportArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeArgument=false, reportUndefinedVariable=false, reportGeneralTypeIssues=false, reportOptionalMemberAccess=false, reportOptionalSubscript=false, reportOptionalIterable=false, reportOptionalCall=false, reportReturnType=false, reportAssignmentType=false, reportOptionalOperand=false, reportUnnecessaryComparison=false, reportUnusedFunction=false, reportUnusedVariable=false, reportUnboundVariable=false, reportUnknownLambdaType=false, reportUnusedClass=false\n","import sqlite3\n","import os\n","\n","DB_PATH = str(Path(WORK_ROOT) / \"data_export\" / \"urban_observatory.db\")\n","Path(DB_PATH).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(DB_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n","\n","conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH)\n","cur = conn.cursor()\n","\n","# ── Create tables ────────────────────────────────────────────\n","cur.executescript(\"\"\"\n","DROP TABLE IF EXISTS readings;\n","DROP TABLE IF EXISTS sensors;\n","DROP TABLE IF EXISTS variables;\n","\n","CREATE TABLE sensors (\n","    sensor_name       TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n","    location_wkt      TEXT,\n","    centroid_lon      REAL,\n","    centroid_lat      REAL,\n","    ground_height     REAL,\n","    sensor_height     REAL,\n","    broker_name       TEXT,\n","    raw_id            TEXT\n",");\n","\n","CREATE TABLE variables (\n","    variable_name     TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n","    units             TEXT,\n","    theme             TEXT\n",");\n","\n","CREATE TABLE readings (\n","    id                INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n","    sensor_name       TEXT NOT NULL,\n","    variable          TEXT NOT NULL,\n","    value             REAL,\n","    timestamp         TEXT NOT NULL,\n","    flagged           INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n","    FOREIGN KEY (sensor_name) REFERENCES sensors(sensor_name),\n","    FOREIGN KEY (variable) REFERENCES variables(variable_name)\n",");\n","\n","CREATE INDEX idx_readings_sensor ON readings(sensor_name);\n","CREATE INDEX idx_readings_variable ON readings(variable);\n","CREATE INDEX idx_readings_ts ON readings(timestamp);\n","\"\"\")\n","\n","# ── Populate sensors table from sensors_df ───────────────────\n","_sensors_df = globals().get('sensors_df')\n","if _sensors_df is not None and not _sensors_df.empty:\n","    # Handle both naming styles: \"Sensor_Name\" (API CSV) and \"Sensor Name\" (parquet)\n","    col_map = {\n","        'Sensor_Name': 'sensor_name',                   'Sensor Name': 'sensor_name',\n","        'Location_WKT': 'location_wkt',                 'Location WKT': 'location_wkt',\n","        'Sensor_Centroid_Longitude': 'centroid_lon',    'Sensor Centroid Longitude': 'centroid_lon',\n","        'Sensor_Centroid_Latitude': 'centroid_lat',     'Sensor Centroid Latitude': 'centroid_lat',\n","        'Ground_Height_Above_Sea_Level': 'ground_height',\n","        'Ground Height Above Sea Level': 'ground_height',\n","        'Sensor_Height_Above_Ground': 'sensor_height',\n","        'Sensor Height Above Ground': 'sensor_height',\n","        'Broker_Name': 'broker_name',                   'Broker Name': 'broker_name',\n","        'Raw_ID': 'raw_id',                             'Raw ID': 'raw_id',\n","    }\n","    s_df = _sensors_df.rename(columns=col_map)\n","    # De-dup columns produced by the merged map (keep first occurrence)\n","    s_df = s_df.loc[:, ~s_df.columns.duplicated()]\n","    available = [c for c in set(col_map.values()) if c in s_df.columns]\n","    if available:\n","        s_df[available].to_sql('sensors', conn, if_exists='replace', index=False)\n","        print(f\"sensors table: {len(s_df)} rows  (cols: {available})\")\n","        # Ensure schema-complete columns exist (NULL when not in source) so the\n","        # benchmark gold SQL referring to broker_name / ground_height / etc.\n","        # always parses. ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN is the SQLite idiom for this.\n","        _expected = ['sensor_name', 'location_wkt', 'centroid_lon', 'centroid_lat',\n","                     'ground_height', 'sensor_height', 'broker_name', 'raw_id']\n","        _existing = {row[1] for row in cur.execute(\"PRAGMA table_info(sensors)\").fetchall()}\n","        for _col in _expected:\n","            if _col not in _existing:\n","                _typ = 'REAL' if _col in ('centroid_lon','centroid_lat','ground_height','sensor_height') else 'TEXT'\n","                cur.execute(f\"ALTER TABLE sensors ADD COLUMN {_col} {_typ}\")\n","        conn.commit()\n","    else:\n","        print(f\"  sensors_df has unknown columns ({list(_sensors_df.columns)}); \"\n","              f\"skipping sensors table population\")\n","\n","# ── Populate variables table from API ────────────────────────\n","_variables = globals().get('variables')\n","if _variables is not None:\n","    var_rows: list[dict[str, str]] = []\n","    for v in _variables.get('Variables', []):\n","        var_rows.append({\n","            'variable_name': v.get('Name', ''),\n","            'units': v.get('Units', ''),\n","            'theme': v.get('Theme', {}).get('Name', '') if isinstance(v.get('Theme'), dict) else str(v.get('Theme', ''))\n","        })\n","    pd.DataFrame(var_rows).to_sql('variables', conn, if_exists='replace', index=False)\n","    print(f\"variables table: {len(var_rows)} rows\")\n","\n","# ── Populate readings table from all fetched DataFrames ──────\n","readings_frames: list[pd.DataFrame] = []\n","for name in ['df_aq', 'df_30d', 'df_history']:\n","    df_tmp = globals().get(name)\n","    if df_tmp is not None and not df_tmp.empty:\n","        readings_frames.append(df_tmp)\n","\n","if readings_frames:\n","    all_readings = pd.concat(readings_frames, ignore_index=True)\n","    # Normalise to underscore-style first (handles both naming styles + the\n","    # snapshot-fallback frames that omit Sensor_Name entirely on cell 20).\n","    rename_map = {\n","        'Sensor_Name': 'sensor_name', 'Sensor Name': 'sensor_name', 'sensor_name': 'sensor_name',\n","        'Variable':    'variable',    'variable':    'variable',\n","        'Value':       'value',       'value':       'value',\n","        'Timestamp':   'timestamp',   'timestamp':   'timestamp',\n","        'Flagged':     'flagged',     'flagged':     'flagged',\n","    }\n","    r_df = all_readings.rename(columns=rename_map)\n","    r_df = r_df.loc[:, ~r_df.columns.duplicated()]\n","    # NOT NULL on sensor_name + variable + timestamp — drop rows missing any\n","    required = [c for c in ('sensor_name', 'variable', 'timestamp') if c in r_df.columns]\n","    if required:\n","        before = len(r_df)\n","        r_df = r_df.dropna(subset=required)\n","        if len(r_df) < before:\n","            print(f\"  dropped {before-len(r_df):,} rows with NULL sensor/variable/timestamp\")\n","    if 'sensor_name' in r_df.columns and 'variable' in r_df.columns and 'timestamp' in r_df.columns:\n","        r_df = r_df.drop_duplicates(subset=['sensor_name', 'variable', 'timestamp'])\n","    cols = ['sensor_name', 'variable', 'value', 'timestamp', 'flagged']\n","    available_cols = [c for c in cols if c in r_df.columns]\n","    if {'sensor_name', 'variable', 'timestamp'}.issubset(available_cols) and len(r_df):\n","        # cast timestamp -> str so SQLite stores ISO text consistently\n","        if 'timestamp' in r_df.columns:\n","            r_df['timestamp'] = r_df['timestamp'].astype(str)\n","        r_df[available_cols].to_sql('readings', conn, if_exists='append', index=False)\n","        print(f\"readings table: {len(r_df):,} rows\")\n","    else:\n","        print(f\"  readings frames missing required columns ({available_cols}); skipping insert\")\n","\n","conn.commit()\n","\n","# ── Verify ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","for table in ['sensors', 'variables', 'readings']:\n","    count = cur.execute(f\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM {table}\").fetchone()[0]\n","    print(f\"  {table}: {count} rows\")\n","\n","conn.close()\n","\n","mirror_save(\"urban_observatory.db\")\n","print(f\"\\nDatabase saved to: {DB_PATH}\")\n","\n","print(f\"Size: {os.path.getsize(DB_PATH) / 1024:.1f} KB\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"64a12473","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.049679,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:55.823068","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:55.773389","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 12. DDL Schema & Prompt Templates\n","\n","The `CREATE TABLE` DDL below is the **exact schema** embedded in LLM prompts.\n","Few-shot prompts include this full DDL (ρ_exposure = 1.0); RAG prompts retrieve subsets."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":27,"id":"a0073164","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-30T04:34:55.929025Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-30T04:34:55.928209Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.137086Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.135431Z"},"papermill":{"duration":3.267836,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.139547","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:55.871711","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  installing tiktoken ...\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Full schema DDL: 136 tokens\n","Schema chunks: sensors=69tok, variables=63tok, readings=75tok\n","Few-shot examples defined: 3\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImports=false, reportUnnecessaryIsInstance=false, reportPrivateImportUsage=false, reportMissingParameterType=false, reportUnusedImport=false, reportArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeArgument=false, reportUndefinedVariable=false, reportGeneralTypeIssues=false, reportOptionalMemberAccess=false, reportOptionalSubscript=false, reportOptionalIterable=false, reportOptionalCall=false, reportReturnType=false, reportAssignmentType=false, reportOptionalOperand=false, reportUnnecessaryComparison=false, reportUnusedFunction=false, reportUnusedVariable=false, reportUnboundVariable=false, reportUnknownLambdaType=false, reportUnusedClass=false\n","# ── Full DDL (used in few-shot prompt) ────────────────────────\n","SCHEMA_DDL = \"\"\"\n","CREATE TABLE sensors (\n","    sensor_name       TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n","    location_wkt      TEXT,\n","    centroid_lon      REAL,\n","    centroid_lat      REAL,\n","    ground_height     REAL,\n","    sensor_height     REAL,\n","    broker_name       TEXT,\n","    raw_id            TEXT\n",");\n","\n","CREATE TABLE variables (\n","    variable_name     TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n","    units             TEXT,\n","    theme             TEXT\n",");\n","\n","CREATE TABLE readings (\n","    id                INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n","    sensor_name       TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES sensors(sensor_name),\n","    variable          TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES variables(variable_name),\n","    value             REAL,\n","    timestamp         TEXT NOT NULL,\n","    flagged           INTEGER DEFAULT 0\n",");\n","\"\"\".strip()\n","\n","# ── Schema chunks for RAG retrieval ──────────────────────────\n","SCHEMA_CHUNKS = {\n","    \"sensors\": \"\"\"CREATE TABLE sensors (\n","    sensor_name TEXT PRIMARY KEY, location_wkt TEXT,\n","    centroid_lon REAL, centroid_lat REAL, ground_height REAL,\n","    sensor_height REAL, broker_name TEXT, raw_id TEXT\n",");\n","-- sensors: one row per physical IoT device. Contains location,\n","-- elevation, broker source. Join to readings on sensor_name.\"\"\",\n","\n","    \"variables\": \"\"\"CREATE TABLE variables (\n","    variable_name TEXT PRIMARY KEY, units TEXT, theme TEXT\n",");\n","-- variables: one row per measurement type (e.g. NO2, PM2.5).\n","-- Theme groups variables (Air Quality, Traffic, Weather, etc.).\n","-- Join to readings on variable = variable_name.\"\"\",\n","\n","    \"readings\": \"\"\"CREATE TABLE readings (\n","    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n","    sensor_name TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES sensors(sensor_name),\n","    variable TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES variables(variable_name),\n","    value REAL, timestamp TEXT NOT NULL, flagged INTEGER DEFAULT 0\n",");\n","-- readings: fact table. One row per sensor × variable × timestamp.\n","-- Contains the actual measured values. Time-series data.\"\"\"\n","}\n","\n","# ── Few-shot worked examples (2 per tier, 10 total) ──────────\n","FEW_SHOT_EXAMPLES = [\n","    {\n","        \"tier\": \"T1\",\n","        \"question\": \"List all sensor names and their broker sources.\",\n","        \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, broker_name FROM sensors;\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"tier\": \"T2\",\n","        \"question\": \"What is the average NO2 value per sensor?\",\n","        \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name;\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"tier\": \"T3\",\n","        \"question\": \"Which sensors recorded PM2.5 readings above 25?\",\n","        \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'PM2.5' AND r.value > 25;\"\n","    },\n","]\n","\n","# ── Prompt templates ─────────────────────────────────────────\n","FEW_SHOT_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a SQL expert. Given the following database schema and examples, write a SQL query for the question.\n","\n","Schema:\n","{schema}\n","\n","Examples:\n","{examples}\n","\n","Question: {question}\n","SQL:\"\"\"\n","\n","RAG_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a SQL expert. Given the following relevant schema fragments, write a SQL query for the question.\n","\n","Relevant Schema:\n","{schema_fragments}\n","\n","Question: {question}\n","SQL:\"\"\"\n","\n","try:\n","    import tiktoken\n","except ImportError:\n","    import subprocess as _sp, sys as _sys\n","    print(\"  installing tiktoken ...\")\n","    _sp.run([_sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", \"tiktoken\"], check=True)\n","    import tiktoken\n","try:\n","    enc = tiktoken.encoding_for_model(\"gpt-4\")\n","except Exception:\n","    enc = tiktoken.get_encoding(\"cl100k_base\")\n","\n","SCHEMA_TOKEN_COUNT = len(enc.encode(SCHEMA_DDL))\n","print(f\"Full schema DDL: {SCHEMA_TOKEN_COUNT} tokens\")\n","print(f\"Schema chunks: {', '.join(f'{k}={len(enc.encode(v))}tok' for k, v in SCHEMA_CHUNKS.items())}\")\n","print(f\"Few-shot examples defined: {len(FEW_SHOT_EXAMPLES)}\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ec44b82c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.053989,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.246023","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.192034","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 13. Benchmark Question Set (T1–T5) — 150 Questions, All Themes\n","\n","**150 NL→SQL question pairs** across 5 complexity tiers (30 per tier), covering **all 15 Urban Observatory themes** (Air Quality, Traffic, Weather, Noise, Water Quality, Environment, Building, …). Questions are grounded in the full 2013-to-present population dataset.\n","\n","| Tier | N | Complexity | SQL Patterns | Decision Level (Anthony, 1965) |\n","|---|---|---|---|---|\n","| T1 | 30 | Single-table lookup | SELECT, WHERE, DISTINCT, LIMIT, COUNT | Operational |\n","| T2 | 30 | Single-table aggregation | GROUP BY, HAVING, aggregate functions, variance approx | Operational |\n","| T3 | 30 | Two-table join | JOIN (exactly 2 tables), subquery in WHERE/HAVING | Managerial |\n","| T4 | 30 | Window / 3-table join | RANK, ROW_NUMBER, LAG, LEAD, NTILE, PERCENT_RANK | Managerial |\n","| T5 | 30 | Multi-CTE cross-theme | WITH … AS chains, cross-variable analysis | Strategic |\n","\n","> **Benchmark validity (Walpole et al., §9.3):** Ground-truth SQL is validated against the full population database. Because we use the complete archive ($N$ = all readings, not a sample), the ground-truth result sets represent true population outcomes — model accuracy proportions are then subject to Wilson CI inference (§19).\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":28,"id":"c81ee5c9","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.359353Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.359016Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.438864Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.437566Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.143026,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.441447","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.298421","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Total benchmark questions: 150\n","  T1: 30 questions | domains: ['air_quality', 'building', 'environment', 'metadata', 'noise', 'traffic', 'water', 'weather']\n","  T2: 30 questions | domains: ['air_quality', 'metadata', 'multi_theme', 'noise', 'traffic', 'water', 'weather']\n","  T3: 30 questions | domains: ['air_quality', 'metadata', 'multi_theme', 'noise', 'traffic', 'weather']\n","  T4: 30 questions | domains: ['air_quality', 'multi_theme', 'noise', 'traffic', 'weather']\n","  T5: 30 questions | domains: ['air_quality', 'multi_theme']\n","\n","Saved to data_export/benchmark_questions.json\n","IDs: ['T1_01', 'T1_02', 'T1_03', 'T1_04', 'T1_05'] … ['T5_28', 'T5_29', 'T5_30']\n"]}],"source":["# pyright: reportUnknownMemberType=false, reportUnknownVariableType=false, reportUnknownArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeStubs=false, reportIndexIssue=false, reportUnknownParameterType=false, reportAttributeAccessIssue=false, reportCallIssue=false, reportOperatorIssue=false, reportConstantRedefinition=false, reportPossiblyUnboundVariable=false, reportMissingImports=false, reportUnnecessaryIsInstance=false, reportPrivateImportUsage=false, reportMissingParameterType=false, reportUnusedImport=false, reportArgumentType=false, reportMissingTypeArgument=false, reportUndefinedVariable=false, reportGeneralTypeIssues=false, reportOptionalMemberAccess=false, reportOptionalSubscript=false, reportOptionalIterable=false, reportOptionalCall=false, reportReturnType=false, reportAssignmentType=false, reportOptionalOperand=false, reportUnnecessaryComparison=false, reportUnusedFunction=false, reportUnusedVariable=false, reportUnboundVariable=false, reportUnknownLambdaType=false, reportUnusedClass=false\n","import json\n","\n","BENCHMARK_QUESTIONS = [\n","\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    # TIER 1 — Single-table lookup (no JOIN, simple aggregation allowed)\n","    # Covers: metadata, all themes\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_01\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all sensor names and their broker sources.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, broker_name FROM sensors;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_02\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many sensors are in the database?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT COUNT(*) AS sensor_count FROM sensors;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_03\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all distinct broker names.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT broker_name FROM sensors;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_04\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What are the variable names that belong to the Air Quality theme?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name, units FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Air Quality';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_05\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all distinct themes in the variables table.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT theme FROM variables ORDER BY theme;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_06\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the centroid latitude and longitude of all sensors.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, centroid_lat, centroid_lon FROM sensors;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_07\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors have a ground height above 50 metres?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, ground_height FROM sensors WHERE ground_height > 50 ORDER BY ground_height DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_08\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many distinct variable types are there across all themes?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT variable_name) AS var_count FROM variables;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_09\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all sensors from the AURN broker.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name FROM sensors WHERE broker_name = 'AURN';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_10\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What units does the NO2 variable use?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT units FROM variables WHERE variable_name = 'NO2';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_11\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"traffic\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all variables in the Traffic theme with their units.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name, units FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Traffic';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_12\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all variables in the Weather theme with their units.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name, units FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Weather';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_13\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all sensors from the Wunderground broker.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name FROM sensors WHERE broker_name = 'Wunderground';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_14\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which variables use µg/m³ as their unit?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name FROM variables WHERE units = 'µg/m³';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_15\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List the 10 northernmost sensors by centroid latitude.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, centroid_lat FROM sensors ORDER BY centroid_lat DESC LIMIT 10;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_16\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"noise\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all variables in the Noise theme with their units.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name, units FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Noise';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_17\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors have a NULL ground height?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name FROM sensors WHERE ground_height IS NULL;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_18\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List sensors located north of latitude 54.98 degrees.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, centroid_lat FROM sensors WHERE centroid_lat > 54.98 ORDER BY centroid_lat DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_19\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all sensors from the AQMesh broker.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name FROM sensors WHERE broker_name = 'AQMesh';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_20\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"water\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all variables in the Water Quality theme with their units.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name, units FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Water Quality';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_21\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors have a sensor height above ground greater than 5 metres?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, sensor_height FROM sensors WHERE sensor_height > 5 ORDER BY sensor_height DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_22\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"traffic\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all variables that use kilometres per hour as their unit.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name FROM variables WHERE units = 'km/h';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_23\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all sensors from the LORA broker.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name FROM sensors WHERE broker_name = 'LORA';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_24\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"environment\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all variables in the Environment theme with their units.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name, units FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Environment';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_25\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the lowest ground height recorded among all sensors?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT MIN(ground_height) AS min_height FROM sensors WHERE ground_height IS NOT NULL;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_26\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List sensors with a ground height between 10 and 30 metres.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, ground_height FROM sensors WHERE ground_height BETWEEN 10 AND 30 ORDER BY ground_height;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_27\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"building\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all variables in the Building theme with their units.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name, units FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Building';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_28\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many distinct themes are represented in the variables table?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT theme) AS theme_count FROM variables;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_29\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List all variable names sorted alphabetically.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable_name, theme, units FROM variables ORDER BY variable_name;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T1_30\", \"tier\": \"T1\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors are located west of longitude −1.64 degrees?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, centroid_lon FROM sensors WHERE centroid_lon < -1.64 ORDER BY centroid_lon;\"},\n","\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    # TIER 2 — Single-table aggregation with GROUP BY\n","    # Covers: all themes, population-level aggregates\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_01\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average NO2 value per sensor over the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_02\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the maximum PM2.5 reading recorded by each sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, MAX(value) AS max_pm25 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM2.5' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY max_pm25 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_03\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many readings does each sensor have in total across all themes?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(*) AS reading_count FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY reading_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_04\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average value for each variable type across all sensors and all time?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable, AVG(value) AS avg_val, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings GROUP BY variable ORDER BY n DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_05\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many sensors belong to each broker?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT broker_name, COUNT(*) AS sensor_count FROM sensors GROUP BY broker_name ORDER BY sensor_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_06\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the daily average NO2 for each sensor over the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) ORDER BY sensor_name, day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_07\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many flagged readings exist per variable across all time?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable, SUM(flagged) AS flagged_count, COUNT(*) AS total, ROUND(100.0*SUM(flagged)/COUNT(*),2) AS pct_flagged FROM readings WHERE flagged = 1 GROUP BY variable ORDER BY flagged_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_08\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the earliest and latest reading timestamp for each sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, MIN(timestamp) AS earliest, MAX(timestamp) AS latest, ROUND(JULIANDAY(MAX(timestamp))-JULIANDAY(MIN(timestamp)),0) AS span_days FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY span_days DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_09\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many variable types exist in each theme?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT theme, COUNT(*) AS var_count FROM variables GROUP BY theme ORDER BY var_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_10\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compute the approximate population variance of NO2 readings per sensor using E[X²] − (E[X])².\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(*) AS n, AVG(value) AS mean_no2, AVG(value*value) - AVG(value)*AVG(value) AS pop_variance FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY pop_variance DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_11\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"traffic\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average Vehicle_Count per sensor over the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_vehicle_count, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Vehicle_Count' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY avg_vehicle_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_12\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many distinct variables does each sensor measure across all themes?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(DISTINCT variable) AS variable_count FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY variable_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_13\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average Temperature reading per sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_temp_c, MIN(value) AS min_temp, MAX(value) AS max_temp FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Temperature' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY avg_temp_c DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_14\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"traffic\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the maximum Vehicle_Count recorded by each sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, MAX(value) AS max_count FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Vehicle_Count' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY max_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_15\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"noise\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average and maximum LAeq_1min noise level per sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_laeq_db, MAX(value) AS max_laeq_db, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings WHERE variable = 'LAeq_1min' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY avg_laeq_db DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_16\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the daily average PM2.5 for each sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_pm25 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM2.5' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) ORDER BY sensor_name, day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_17\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many readings were recorded per calendar year across all themes?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT strftime('%Y', timestamp) AS year, COUNT(*) AS reading_count, COUNT(DISTINCT variable) AS n_variables FROM readings GROUP BY strftime('%Y', timestamp) ORDER BY year;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_18\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many readings were recorded per hour of the day (0–23) across the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT CAST(strftime('%H', timestamp) AS INTEGER) AS hour, COUNT(*) AS reading_count FROM readings GROUP BY strftime('%H', timestamp) ORDER BY hour;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_19\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many non-flagged (clean) readings exist per variable?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT variable, COUNT(*) AS clean_count FROM readings WHERE flagged = 0 GROUP BY variable ORDER BY clean_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_20\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average Wind_Speed per sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_wind_mps, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Wind_Speed' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY avg_wind_mps DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_21\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the total flagged reading count and flagging percentage per sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, SUM(flagged) AS total_flagged, COUNT(*) AS total, ROUND(100.0*SUM(flagged)/COUNT(*),2) AS pct_flagged FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY pct_flagged DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_22\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average Relative_Humidity per sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_rh_pct, MIN(value) AS min_rh, MAX(value) AS max_rh FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Relative_Humidity' GROUP BY sensor_name;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_23\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the data span in days for each sensor (max − min timestamp)?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, ROUND(JULIANDAY(MAX(timestamp)) - JULIANDAY(MIN(timestamp)), 1) AS span_days FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY span_days DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_24\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"water\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the maximum River_Level recorded per sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, MAX(value) AS max_river_level, AVG(value) AS mean_level FROM readings WHERE variable = 'River_Level' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY max_river_level DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_25\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many readings were recorded per calendar month (year-month) across all themes?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT strftime('%Y-%m', timestamp) AS month, COUNT(*) AS reading_count FROM readings GROUP BY strftime('%Y-%m', timestamp) ORDER BY month;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_26\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the overall minimum and maximum NO2 value recorded across all sensors in the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT MIN(value) AS min_no2, MAX(value) AS max_no2, AVG(value) AS mean_no2, COUNT(*) AS total_readings FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2';\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_27\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average Atmospheric_Pressure per sensor?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_pressure_hpa FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Atmospheric_Pressure' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY avg_pressure_hpa DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_28\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the cumulative total Rainfall per sensor over the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, SUM(value) AS total_rainfall_mm, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Rainfall' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY total_rainfall_mm DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_29\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many distinct days have NO2 readings per sensor across the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(DISTINCT DATE(timestamp)) AS days_with_data FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY days_with_data DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T2_30\", \"tier\": \"T2\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compute the approximate population variance of PM10 readings per sensor using E[X²] − (E[X])².\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(*) AS n, AVG(value) AS mean_pm10, AVG(value*value) - AVG(value)*AVG(value) AS pop_variance_pm10 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM10' GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY pop_variance_pm10 DESC;\"},\n","\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    # TIER 3 — Exactly two-table JOIN (sensors+readings OR variables+readings)\n","    # Covers: all themes, broker-level analysis\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_01\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors recorded PM2.5 readings above 25 µg/m³? Show sensor name and broker.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'PM2.5' AND r.value > 25;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_02\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average NO2 reading per broker source over the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_03\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"metadata\",\n","     \"question\": \"List the units for each variable that has at least one reading in the database.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT v.variable_name, v.theme, v.units FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable ORDER BY v.theme, v.variable_name;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_04\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which brokers have sensors that recorded flagged readings?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT s.broker_name, COUNT(*) AS flagged_count FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.flagged = 1 GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY flagged_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_05\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"How many readings exist per theme across the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT v.theme, COUNT(*) AS reading_count FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable GROUP BY v.theme ORDER BY reading_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_06\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the average value of each variable along with its theme and units.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT v.variable_name, v.theme, v.units, AVG(r.value) AS avg_val, COUNT(*) AS n FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable GROUP BY v.variable_name, v.theme, v.units ORDER BY v.theme, v.variable_name;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_07\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the total number of readings per sensor, including the broker name?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name, COUNT(*) AS total_readings FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.sensor_name, s.broker_name ORDER BY total_readings DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_08\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Find sensors whose mean NO2 exceeds the overall population mean NO2 across all sensors.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_no2 FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY s.sensor_name, s.broker_name HAVING AVG(r.value) > (SELECT AVG(value) FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2') ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_09\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"List the top 10 sensors by number of distinct variable types they measure.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT r.sensor_name, COUNT(DISTINCT r.variable) AS var_count FROM readings r GROUP BY r.sensor_name ORDER BY var_count DESC LIMIT 10;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_10\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"traffic\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average Vehicle_Count per broker over the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_vehicle_count, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'Vehicle_Count' GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY avg_vehicle_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_11\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which brokers provide the highest average Temperature readings?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_temp_c, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'Temperature' GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY avg_temp_c DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_12\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors have flagged NO2 readings? Show sensor name and broker.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' AND r.flagged = 1;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_13\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average PM10 per broker?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_pm10, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'PM10' GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY avg_pm10 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_14\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors measure both NO2 and Vehicle_Count (multi-theme sensors)?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT r1.sensor_name FROM readings r1 WHERE r1.variable = 'NO2' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM readings r2 WHERE r2.sensor_name = r1.sensor_name AND r2.variable = 'Vehicle_Count');\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_15\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show variable names, themes, and units for variables with more than 1000 readings in the archive.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT v.variable_name, v.theme, v.units, COUNT(r.id) AS reading_count FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable GROUP BY v.variable_name, v.theme, v.units HAVING COUNT(r.id) > 1000 ORDER BY reading_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_16\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the most recent reading timestamp per broker?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, MAX(r.timestamp) AS latest_reading FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY latest_reading DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_17\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"noise\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors have an average LAeq_1min noise level above 60 dB? Show broker.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_laeq_db FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'LAeq_1min' GROUP BY s.sensor_name, s.broker_name HAVING AVG(r.value) > 60 ORDER BY avg_laeq_db DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_18\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compare average NO2 between elevated sensors (ground_height > 10 m) and ground-level sensors.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT CASE WHEN s.ground_height > 10 THEN 'Elevated (>10m)' ELSE 'Ground (≤10m)' END AS elevation_class, AVG(r.value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' AND s.ground_height IS NOT NULL GROUP BY elevation_class;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_19\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which sensors have more than 10000 NO2 readings in the full archive?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name, COUNT(*) AS no2_count FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY s.sensor_name, s.broker_name HAVING COUNT(*) > 10000 ORDER BY no2_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_20\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which variables have an average value above the overall mean of all readings across all variables?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT v.variable_name, v.theme, v.units, AVG(r.value) AS avg_val FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable GROUP BY v.variable_name, v.theme, v.units HAVING AVG(r.value) > (SELECT AVG(value) FROM readings) ORDER BY avg_val DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_21\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average Wind_Speed per broker?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_wind_mps, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'Wind_Speed' GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY avg_wind_mps DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_22\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which brokers have sensors with a data archive spanning more than 365 days?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, s.sensor_name, ROUND(JULIANDAY(MAX(r.timestamp)) - JULIANDAY(MIN(r.timestamp)), 0) AS span_days FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.broker_name, s.sensor_name HAVING span_days > 365 ORDER BY span_days DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_23\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average Relative_Humidity per broker?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_rh_pct, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'Relative_Humidity' GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY avg_rh_pct DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_24\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each sensor and broker, what percentage of readings are flagged?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name, ROUND(100.0 * SUM(r.flagged) / COUNT(*), 2) AS pct_flagged FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.sensor_name, s.broker_name ORDER BY pct_flagged DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_25\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"What is the average of daily maximum NO2 values per broker (average worst-day NO2)?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, AVG(daily_max) AS avg_daily_peak_no2 FROM (SELECT r.sensor_name, DATE(r.timestamp) AS day, MAX(r.value) AS daily_max FROM readings r WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY r.sensor_name, DATE(r.timestamp)) d JOIN sensors s ON d.sensor_name = s.sensor_name GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY avg_daily_peak_no2 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_26\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Which broker has the earliest archive start date?\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.broker_name, MIN(r.timestamp) AS archive_start FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.broker_name ORDER BY archive_start;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_27\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show each variable's theme, its reading count, and average value in the archive.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT v.variable_name, v.theme, COUNT(r.id) AS reading_count, ROUND(AVG(r.value), 4) AS avg_val FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable GROUP BY v.variable_name, v.theme ORDER BY reading_count DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_28\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show average NO2 per sensor with their geographic coordinates.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.sensor_name, s.centroid_lat, s.centroid_lon, AVG(r.value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY s.sensor_name, s.centroid_lat, s.centroid_lon ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_29\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each sensor, show the broker name and the date of its first ever reading in the archive.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name, MIN(r.timestamp) AS first_reading FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.sensor_name, s.broker_name ORDER BY first_reading;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T3_30\", \"tier\": \"T3\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compare average PM2.5 between high-mounted sensors (sensor_height > 3 m) and low-mounted sensors.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT CASE WHEN s.sensor_height > 3 THEN 'High-mount (>3m)' ELSE 'Low-mount (≤3m)' END AS mount_class, AVG(r.value) AS avg_pm25, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'PM2.5' AND s.sensor_height IS NOT NULL GROUP BY mount_class;\"},\n","\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    # TIER 4 — Window functions OR 3-table JOINs\n","    # Covers: all themes, temporal patterns, ranking, running aggregates\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_01\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Rank sensors by their worst (highest) monthly average NO2 over the full archive.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, month, avg_no2, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC) AS overall_rank FROM (SELECT r.sensor_name, strftime('%Y-%m', r.timestamp) AS month, AVG(r.value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings r WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY r.sensor_name, strftime('%Y-%m', r.timestamp)) sub ORDER BY overall_rank;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_02\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each broker, identify the sensor with the highest average PM2.5.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT broker_name, sensor_name, avg_pm25 FROM (SELECT s.broker_name, r.sensor_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_pm25, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY s.broker_name ORDER BY AVG(r.value) DESC) AS rn FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'PM2.5' GROUP BY s.broker_name, r.sensor_name) sub WHERE rn = 1;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_03\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show each NO2 reading alongside the 7-reading rolling average for that sensor.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT r.sensor_name, r.timestamp, r.value, AVG(r.value) OVER (PARTITION BY r.sensor_name ORDER BY r.timestamp ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS rolling_7_avg FROM readings r WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' ORDER BY r.sensor_name, r.timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_04\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each theme, identify the variable with the most readings and show its units.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT theme, variable_name, units, reading_count FROM (SELECT v.theme, v.variable_name, v.units, COUNT(*) AS reading_count, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY v.theme ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) AS rn FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable GROUP BY v.theme, v.variable_name, v.units) sub WHERE rn = 1;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_05\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compute the percentile rank of each sensor's mean NO2 across all sensors.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, avg_no2, ROUND(PERCENT_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY avg_no2) * 100, 2) AS percentile FROM (SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name) sub;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_06\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Find the day-over-day change in average NO2 for each sensor using LAG.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, day, avg_no2, ROUND(avg_no2 - LAG(avg_no2) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY day), 4) AS daily_change FROM (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)) sub ORDER BY sensor_name, day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_07\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each broker, identify the sensor with the longest continuous data archive.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT broker_name, sensor_name, data_span_days FROM (SELECT s.broker_name, r.sensor_name, ROUND(JULIANDAY(MAX(r.timestamp)) - JULIANDAY(MIN(r.timestamp)), 1) AS data_span_days, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY s.broker_name ORDER BY JULIANDAY(MAX(r.timestamp)) - JULIANDAY(MIN(r.timestamp)) DESC) AS rn FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.broker_name, r.sensor_name) sub WHERE rn = 1;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_08\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Classify each sensor-day's average NO2 as Good (<40 µg/m³), Moderate (40–100), or Poor (>100).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, day, avg_no2, CASE WHEN avg_no2 < 40 THEN 'Good' WHEN avg_no2 <= 100 THEN 'Moderate' ELSE 'Poor' END AS aq_class FROM (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)) sub ORDER BY sensor_name, day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_09\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show each NO2 reading's deviation from its sensor's long-term mean (mean-centred values).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT r.sensor_name, r.timestamp, r.value, r.value - AVG(r.value) OVER (PARTITION BY r.sensor_name) AS deviation FROM readings r WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' ORDER BY r.sensor_name, r.timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_10\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each sensor, find the hour of day (0–23) with the highest average NO2.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, hour, avg_no2 FROM (SELECT sensor_name, CAST(strftime('%H', timestamp) AS INTEGER) AS hour, AVG(value) AS avg_no2, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY AVG(value) DESC) AS rn FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, strftime('%H', timestamp)) sub WHERE rn = 1 ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_11\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"traffic\",\n","     \"question\": \"Rank sensors within each broker by their average Vehicle_Count.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT broker_name, sensor_name, avg_count, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY broker_name ORDER BY avg_count DESC) AS broker_rank FROM (SELECT s.broker_name, r.sensor_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_count FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'Vehicle_Count' GROUP BY s.broker_name, r.sensor_name) sub ORDER BY broker_name, broker_rank;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_12\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show each Temperature reading alongside the 24-reading rolling average for that sensor.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT r.sensor_name, r.timestamp, r.value, AVG(r.value) OVER (PARTITION BY r.sensor_name ORDER BY r.timestamp ROWS BETWEEN 23 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS rolling_24_avg FROM readings r WHERE r.variable = 'Temperature' ORDER BY r.sensor_name, r.timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_13\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Find the day-over-day change in average PM2.5 per sensor using LAG.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, day, avg_pm25, ROUND(avg_pm25 - LAG(avg_pm25) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY day), 4) AS daily_change FROM (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_pm25 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM2.5' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)) sub ORDER BY sensor_name, day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_14\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the cumulative total Rainfall per sensor ordered by timestamp (running sum).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, timestamp, value, SUM(value) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY timestamp) AS cumulative_rainfall_mm FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Rainfall' ORDER BY sensor_name, timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_15\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"traffic\",\n","     \"question\": \"Classify each Vehicle_Count reading as Low (<200), Medium (200–600), or High (>600).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, timestamp, value, CASE WHEN value < 200 THEN 'Low' WHEN value <= 600 THEN 'Medium' ELSE 'High' END AS traffic_class FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Vehicle_Count' ORDER BY sensor_name, timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_16\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"noise\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the running minimum and maximum LAeq_1min noise level per sensor.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, timestamp, value, MIN(value) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY timestamp) AS running_min_db, MAX(value) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY timestamp) AS running_max_db FROM readings WHERE variable = 'LAeq_1min' ORDER BY sensor_name, timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_17\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Assign each sensor to a NO2 quartile (NTILE 4) based on its mean NO2.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, avg_no2, NTILE(4) OVER (ORDER BY avg_no2) AS no2_quartile FROM (SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name) sub ORDER BY no2_quartile, avg_no2;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_18\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Find the week-over-week change in average NO2 per sensor using LAG.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, week, avg_no2, ROUND(avg_no2 - LAG(avg_no2) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY week), 4) AS weekly_change FROM (SELECT sensor_name, strftime('%Y-%W', timestamp) AS week, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, strftime('%Y-%W', timestamp)) sub ORDER BY sensor_name, week;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_19\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"noise\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each sensor, find the 3 noisiest hours of the day (by average LAeq_1min).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, hour, avg_laeq_db FROM (SELECT sensor_name, CAST(strftime('%H', timestamp) AS INTEGER) AS hour, AVG(value) AS avg_laeq_db, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY AVG(value) DESC) AS rn FROM readings WHERE variable = 'LAeq_1min' GROUP BY sensor_name, strftime('%H', timestamp)) sub WHERE rn <= 3 ORDER BY sensor_name, rn;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_20\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compute the percentile rank of each sensor's mean PM2.5 within its broker group.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT broker_name, sensor_name, avg_pm25, ROUND(PERCENT_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY broker_name ORDER BY avg_pm25) * 100, 2) AS pct_rank_within_broker FROM (SELECT s.broker_name, r.sensor_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_pm25 FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'PM2.5' GROUP BY s.broker_name, r.sensor_name) sub ORDER BY broker_name, pct_rank_within_broker;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_21\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each theme, identify the variable with the lowest average value.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT theme, variable_name, avg_val FROM (SELECT v.theme, v.variable_name, AVG(r.value) AS avg_val, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY v.theme ORDER BY AVG(r.value) ASC) AS rn FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable GROUP BY v.theme, v.variable_name) sub WHERE rn = 1 ORDER BY theme;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_22\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each sensor show today's average NO2 alongside the predicted next day using LEAD.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, day, avg_no2, LEAD(avg_no2) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY day) AS next_day_no2 FROM (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)) sub ORDER BY sensor_name, day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_23\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each sensor, count the number of distinct calendar years with readings and rank sensors by coverage.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(DISTINCT strftime('%Y', timestamp)) AS years_active, ROUND(JULIANDAY(MAX(timestamp)) - JULIANDAY(MIN(timestamp)), 0) AS archive_span_days, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY COUNT(DISTINCT strftime('%Y', timestamp)) DESC) AS coverage_rank FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY coverage_rank;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_24\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"weather\",\n","     \"question\": \"Classify each Wind_Speed reading as Calm (<5 m/s), Breeze (5–15), Strong (15–30), or Storm (>30).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, timestamp, value, CASE WHEN value < 5 THEN 'Calm' WHEN value < 15 THEN 'Breeze' WHEN value < 30 THEN 'Strong' ELSE 'Storm' END AS wind_class FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Wind_Speed' ORDER BY sensor_name, timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_25\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the monthly NO2 average per sensor alongside the previous month's value using LAG.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, month, avg_no2, ROUND(avg_no2 - LAG(avg_no2) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY month), 4) AS mom_change FROM (SELECT sensor_name, strftime('%Y-%m', timestamp) AS month, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, strftime('%Y-%m', timestamp)) sub ORDER BY sensor_name, month;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_26\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each NO2 reading, show the sensor-level population mean and population variance as window functions.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, timestamp, value, AVG(value) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name) AS sensor_pop_mean, AVG(value*value) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name) - AVG(value) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name) * AVG(value) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name) AS sensor_pop_variance FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' ORDER BY sensor_name, timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_27\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the running cumulative count of flagged readings per sensor per variable.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, variable, timestamp, flagged, SUM(flagged) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name, variable ORDER BY timestamp) AS cumulative_flags FROM readings ORDER BY sensor_name, variable, timestamp;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_28\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Within each broker, rank sensors by total flagged reading count.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT broker_name, sensor_name, total_flagged, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY broker_name ORDER BY total_flagged DESC) AS flagged_rank FROM (SELECT s.broker_name, r.sensor_name, SUM(r.flagged) AS total_flagged FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.broker_name, r.sensor_name) sub ORDER BY broker_name, flagged_rank;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_29\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"traffic\",\n","     \"question\": \"Assign each hour of the day (0–23) to a Vehicle_Count quintile (NTILE 5).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT hour, avg_count, NTILE(5) OVER (ORDER BY avg_count) AS count_quintile FROM (SELECT CAST(strftime('%H', timestamp) AS INTEGER) AS hour, AVG(value) AS avg_count FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Vehicle_Count' GROUP BY strftime('%H', timestamp)) sub ORDER BY hour;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T4_30\", \"tier\": \"T4\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each NO2 reading, classify as Weekday or Weekend and show the group average as a window function.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"SELECT sensor_name, timestamp, value, CASE WHEN CAST(strftime('%w', timestamp) AS INTEGER) IN (0, 6) THEN 'Weekend' ELSE 'Weekday' END AS day_type, AVG(value) OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name, CASE WHEN CAST(strftime('%w', timestamp) AS INTEGER) IN (0, 6) THEN 'Weekend' ELSE 'Weekday' END) AS day_type_mean_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' ORDER BY sensor_name, timestamp;\"},\n","\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    # TIER 5 — Multi-CTE cross-theme strategic analysis (population-level)\n","    # Covers: all themes, long-term trends, cross-variable, strategic decisions\n","    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_01\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compare daily average NO2 and PM2.5 at each sensor on the same day.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH no2 AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)), pm25 AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_pm25 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM2.5' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)) SELECT no2.sensor_name, no2.day, no2.avg_no2, pm25.avg_pm25 FROM no2 JOIN pm25 ON no2.sensor_name = pm25.sensor_name AND no2.day = pm25.day ORDER BY no2.sensor_name, no2.day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_02\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Find days where sensor-level daily average NO2 exceeds 40 µg/m³ AND PM10 exceeds 50 µg/m³ simultaneously.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH no2_high AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) HAVING AVG(value) > 40), pm10_high AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_pm10 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM10' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) HAVING AVG(value) > 50) SELECT n.sensor_name, n.day, n.avg_no2, p.avg_pm10 FROM no2_high n JOIN pm10_high p ON n.sensor_name = p.sensor_name AND n.day = p.day ORDER BY n.day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_03\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each broker, compare the total count of Air Quality readings vs Weather readings.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH aq AS (SELECT s.broker_name, COUNT(*) AS aq_count FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name JOIN variables v ON r.variable = v.variable_name WHERE v.theme = 'Air Quality' GROUP BY s.broker_name), wx AS (SELECT s.broker_name, COUNT(*) AS wx_count FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name JOIN variables v ON r.variable = v.variable_name WHERE v.theme = 'Weather' GROUP BY s.broker_name), brokers AS (SELECT broker_name FROM aq UNION SELECT broker_name FROM wx) SELECT b.broker_name AS broker, COALESCE(aq.aq_count, 0) AS aq_readings, COALESCE(wx.wx_count, 0) AS weather_readings FROM brokers b LEFT JOIN aq ON b.broker_name = aq.broker_name LEFT JOIN wx ON b.broker_name = wx.broker_name ORDER BY aq_readings DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_04\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Identify the top 3 sensors with the most overlapping NO2 and PM2.5 daily observation days (proxy for co-location correlation study).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH daily AS (SELECT r.sensor_name, DATE(r.timestamp) AS day, r.variable, AVG(r.value) AS avg_val FROM readings r WHERE r.variable IN ('NO2', 'PM2.5') GROUP BY r.sensor_name, DATE(r.timestamp), r.variable), pivoted AS (SELECT d1.sensor_name, d1.day, d1.avg_val AS no2_val, d2.avg_val AS pm25_val FROM daily d1 JOIN daily d2 ON d1.sensor_name = d2.sensor_name AND d1.day = d2.day AND d1.variable = 'NO2' AND d2.variable = 'PM2.5') SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(*) AS overlap_days, AVG(no2_val) AS mean_no2, AVG(pm25_val) AS mean_pm25 FROM pivoted GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY overlap_days DESC LIMIT 3;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_05\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Produce a theme-level summary: total unique sensors, total readings, population mean value, and data span in days.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH theme_stats AS (SELECT v.theme, COUNT(DISTINCT r.sensor_name) AS n_sensors, COUNT(*) AS n_readings, AVG(r.value) AS pop_mean, JULIANDAY(MAX(r.timestamp)) - JULIANDAY(MIN(r.timestamp)) AS span_days FROM variables v JOIN readings r ON v.variable_name = r.variable GROUP BY v.theme) SELECT * FROM theme_stats ORDER BY n_readings DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_06\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Find sensor-days where at least 3 different Air Quality variables all exceeded their population mean simultaneously.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH pop_means AS (SELECT variable, AVG(value) AS pop_mean FROM readings WHERE variable IN (SELECT variable_name FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Air Quality') GROUP BY variable), daily_avgs AS (SELECT r.sensor_name, DATE(r.timestamp) AS day, r.variable, AVG(r.value) AS daily_avg FROM readings r WHERE r.variable IN (SELECT variable_name FROM variables WHERE theme = 'Air Quality') GROUP BY r.sensor_name, DATE(r.timestamp), r.variable), exceed AS (SELECT da.sensor_name, da.day, da.variable FROM daily_avgs da JOIN pop_means pm ON da.variable = pm.variable WHERE da.daily_avg > pm.pop_mean) SELECT sensor_name, day, COUNT(DISTINCT variable) AS vars_exceeded FROM exceed GROUP BY sensor_name, day HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT variable) >= 3 ORDER BY day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_07\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"For each sensor, compute the ratio of NO2 readings to total readings and rank sensors by this specialisation ratio.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH totals AS (SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(*) AS total FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name), no2_counts AS (SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(*) AS no2_total FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name) SELECT t.sensor_name, COALESCE(n.no2_total, 0) AS no2_readings, t.total AS total_readings, ROUND(CAST(COALESCE(n.no2_total, 0) AS REAL) / t.total, 4) AS no2_ratio, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY CAST(COALESCE(n.no2_total, 0) AS REAL) / t.total DESC) AS ratio_rank FROM totals t LEFT JOIN no2_counts n ON t.sensor_name = n.sensor_name ORDER BY ratio_rank;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_08\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compare the hourly NO2 profile between AURN sensors and all other broker sensors.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH hourly AS (SELECT CASE WHEN s.broker_name = 'AURN' THEN 'AURN' ELSE 'Non-AURN' END AS source, CAST(strftime('%H', r.timestamp) AS INTEGER) AS hour, AVG(r.value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY source, strftime('%H', r.timestamp)) SELECT source, hour, avg_no2, n FROM hourly ORDER BY source, hour;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_09\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Find the top 5 days with the worst multi-pollutant air quality index (sum of normalised daily NO2 and PM2.5 averages).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH no2_stats AS (SELECT AVG(value) AS mu, MAX(value) - MIN(value) AS range_val FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2'), pm25_stats AS (SELECT AVG(value) AS mu, MAX(value) - MIN(value) AS range_val FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM2.5'), daily AS (SELECT DATE(timestamp) AS day, variable, AVG(value) AS avg_val FROM readings WHERE variable IN ('NO2', 'PM2.5') GROUP BY DATE(timestamp), variable), normed AS (SELECT d.day, d.variable, CASE WHEN d.variable = 'NO2' THEN (d.avg_val - ns.mu) / NULLIF(ns.range_val, 0) ELSE (d.avg_val - ps.mu) / NULLIF(ps.range_val, 0) END AS norm_val FROM daily d, no2_stats ns, pm25_stats ps) SELECT day, SUM(norm_val) AS multi_pollutant_index FROM normed GROUP BY day ORDER BY multi_pollutant_index DESC LIMIT 5;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_10\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Generate a cross-tabulation of brokers vs themes, showing the count of readings in each cell.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH base AS (SELECT s.broker_name, v.theme, COUNT(*) AS cnt FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name JOIN variables v ON r.variable = v.variable_name GROUP BY s.broker_name, v.theme) SELECT broker_name, theme, cnt FROM base ORDER BY broker_name, theme;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_11\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Identify sensors that measure both Traffic and Air Quality themes, comparing their data volumes.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH aq_sensors AS (SELECT DISTINCT r.sensor_name FROM readings r JOIN variables v ON r.variable = v.variable_name WHERE v.theme = 'Air Quality'), traffic_sensors AS (SELECT DISTINCT r.sensor_name FROM readings r JOIN variables v ON r.variable = v.variable_name WHERE v.theme = 'Traffic'), both_sensors AS (SELECT a.sensor_name FROM aq_sensors a JOIN traffic_sensors t ON a.sensor_name = t.sensor_name) SELECT b.sensor_name, SUM(CASE WHEN v.theme = 'Air Quality' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS aq_readings, SUM(CASE WHEN v.theme = 'Traffic' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS traffic_readings FROM both_sensors b JOIN readings r ON b.sensor_name = r.sensor_name JOIN variables v ON r.variable = v.variable_name GROUP BY b.sensor_name ORDER BY aq_readings + traffic_readings DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_12\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the year-over-year change in average NO2 across all sensors (2013–present) with percentage change.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH yearly AS (SELECT strftime('%Y', timestamp) AS year, AVG(value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n_readings FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY strftime('%Y', timestamp)) SELECT year, avg_no2, n_readings, ROUND(avg_no2 - LAG(avg_no2) OVER (ORDER BY year), 4) AS yoy_change, ROUND(100.0 * (avg_no2 - LAG(avg_no2) OVER (ORDER BY year)) / NULLIF(LAG(avg_no2) OVER (ORDER BY year), 0), 2) AS pct_change FROM yearly ORDER BY year;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_13\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Identify multi-theme sensors that measure at least 3 distinct themes, ranked by theme breadth.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH sensor_themes AS (SELECT r.sensor_name, v.theme FROM readings r JOIN variables v ON r.variable = v.variable_name GROUP BY r.sensor_name, v.theme), theme_count AS (SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(DISTINCT theme) AS n_themes, GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT theme) AS theme_list FROM sensor_themes GROUP BY sensor_name) SELECT s.sensor_name, s.broker_name, tc.n_themes, tc.theme_list FROM sensors s JOIN theme_count tc ON s.sensor_name = tc.sensor_name WHERE tc.n_themes >= 3 ORDER BY tc.n_themes DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_14\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Seasonal analysis of NO2 (DJF=Winter, MAM=Spring, JJA=Summer, SON=Autumn) per sensor across the full archive.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH seasonal AS (SELECT sensor_name, CASE WHEN CAST(strftime('%m', timestamp) AS INTEGER) IN (12, 1, 2) THEN 'DJF-Winter' WHEN CAST(strftime('%m', timestamp) AS INTEGER) IN (3, 4, 5) THEN 'MAM-Spring' WHEN CAST(strftime('%m', timestamp) AS INTEGER) IN (6, 7, 8) THEN 'JJA-Summer' ELSE 'SON-Autumn' END AS season, AVG(value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, season) SELECT sensor_name, season, avg_no2, n, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY sensor_name ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC) AS season_rank FROM seasonal ORDER BY sensor_name, avg_no2 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_15\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Detect sensor-days where NO2, PM2.5, and LAeq_1min all simultaneously exceed their population means (multi-theme pollution events).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH pop_means AS (SELECT variable, AVG(value) AS pop_mean FROM readings WHERE variable IN ('NO2', 'PM2.5', 'LAeq_1min') GROUP BY variable), daily_avgs AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, variable, AVG(value) AS daily_avg FROM readings WHERE variable IN ('NO2', 'PM2.5', 'LAeq_1min') GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp), variable), exceed AS (SELECT da.sensor_name, da.day, da.variable FROM daily_avgs da JOIN pop_means pm ON da.variable = pm.variable WHERE da.daily_avg > pm.pop_mean) SELECT sensor_name, day, COUNT(DISTINCT variable) AS n_exceeding FROM exceed GROUP BY sensor_name, day HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT variable) = 3 ORDER BY day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_16\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compute average NO2 stratified by sensor ground elevation tier (0–10 m, 10–20 m, 20 m+, Unknown).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH elevation_tiers AS (SELECT s.sensor_name, CASE WHEN s.ground_height IS NULL THEN 'Unknown' WHEN s.ground_height < 10 THEN '0-10m' WHEN s.ground_height < 20 THEN '10-20m' ELSE '20m+' END AS elev_tier FROM sensors s), tier_avg AS (SELECT et.elev_tier, AVG(r.value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n FROM elevation_tiers et JOIN readings r ON et.sensor_name = r.sensor_name WHERE r.variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY et.elev_tier) SELECT elev_tier, avg_no2, n, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC) AS tier_rank FROM tier_avg ORDER BY avg_no2 DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_17\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Traffic-to-AQ interaction: compare hourly average Vehicle_Count with hourly average NO2 to detect temporal lag patterns.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH hourly_traffic AS (SELECT CAST(strftime('%H', timestamp) AS INTEGER) AS hour, AVG(value) AS avg_traffic, COUNT(*) AS n_traffic FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Vehicle_Count' GROUP BY strftime('%H', timestamp)), hourly_no2 AS (SELECT CAST(strftime('%H', timestamp) AS INTEGER) AS hour, AVG(value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY strftime('%H', timestamp)) SELECT t.hour, t.avg_traffic, n.avg_no2, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY t.avg_traffic DESC) AS traffic_rank, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY n.avg_no2 DESC) AS no2_rank FROM hourly_traffic t JOIN hourly_no2 n ON t.hour = n.hour ORDER BY t.hour;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_18\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Sensor health audit: for each sensor and theme, compute total readings, flagged count, and flagging rate.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH flag_rates AS (SELECT r.sensor_name, v.theme, COUNT(*) AS total, SUM(r.flagged) AS n_flagged, ROUND(100.0 * SUM(r.flagged) / COUNT(*), 2) AS pct_flagged FROM readings r JOIN variables v ON r.variable = v.variable_name GROUP BY r.sensor_name, v.theme) SELECT f.sensor_name, s.broker_name, f.theme, f.total, f.n_flagged, f.pct_flagged FROM flag_rates f JOIN sensors s ON f.sensor_name = s.sensor_name ORDER BY f.pct_flagged DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_19\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Population-period comparison: compare mean NO2 for the pre-2020 period (2013–2019) vs post-2020 period (2020–present) per sensor.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH pre2020 AS (SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS mean_no2_pre, COUNT(*) AS n_pre FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' AND timestamp < '2020-01-01' GROUP BY sensor_name), post2020 AS (SELECT sensor_name, AVG(value) AS mean_no2_post, COUNT(*) AS n_post FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' AND timestamp >= '2020-01-01' GROUP BY sensor_name) SELECT COALESCE(a.sensor_name, b.sensor_name) AS sensor_name, a.n_pre, a.mean_no2_pre, b.n_post, b.mean_no2_post, ROUND(b.mean_no2_post - a.mean_no2_pre, 4) AS period_change FROM pre2020 a LEFT JOIN post2020 b ON a.sensor_name = b.sensor_name ORDER BY period_change;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_20\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compute a composite air quality index per sensor per day as a weighted sum of normalised NO2 (40%), PM2.5 (35%), and PM10 (25%).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH daily_no2 AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)), daily_pm25 AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_pm25 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM2.5' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)), daily_pm10 AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_pm10 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'PM10' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)) SELECT COALESCE(n.sensor_name, p.sensor_name, q.sensor_name) AS sensor_name, COALESCE(n.day, p.day, q.day) AS day, ROUND(COALESCE(n.avg_no2, 0) * 0.4 + COALESCE(p.avg_pm25, 0) * 0.35 + COALESCE(q.avg_pm10, 0) * 0.25, 3) AS composite_aqi FROM daily_no2 n LEFT JOIN daily_pm25 p ON n.sensor_name = p.sensor_name AND n.day = p.day LEFT JOIN daily_pm10 q ON n.sensor_name = q.sensor_name AND n.day = q.day ORDER BY composite_aqi DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_21\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the annual reading volume per sensor from 2013 to 2026, summarised as a year-coverage profile.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH year_coverage AS (SELECT sensor_name, strftime('%Y', timestamp) AS year, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name, strftime('%Y', timestamp)) SELECT sensor_name, GROUP_CONCAT(year || ':' || n, ' | ') AS annual_profile, COUNT(DISTINCT year) AS years_active, SUM(n) AS total_readings FROM year_coverage GROUP BY sensor_name ORDER BY years_active DESC, total_readings DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_22\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Broker reliability report: rank brokers by their clean (non-flagged) reading percentage over the full archive.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH broker_quality AS (SELECT s.broker_name, COUNT(*) AS total, SUM(CASE WHEN r.flagged = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS clean FROM sensors s JOIN readings r ON s.sensor_name = r.sensor_name GROUP BY s.broker_name) SELECT broker_name, total, clean, ROUND(100.0 * clean / total, 2) AS pct_clean, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY 100.0 * clean / total DESC) AS quality_rank FROM broker_quality ORDER BY quality_rank;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_23\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Identify the top 10 sensors by a composite dataset completeness score (clean reading %, day coverage %, and variable breadth).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH coverage AS (SELECT sensor_name, COUNT(DISTINCT DATE(timestamp)) AS active_days, ROUND(JULIANDAY(MAX(timestamp)) - JULIANDAY(MIN(timestamp)), 0) AS span_days, COUNT(DISTINCT variable) AS n_vars, ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN flagged = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*), 2) AS pct_clean FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name), scored AS (SELECT c.sensor_name, s.broker_name, c.pct_clean, c.active_days, c.span_days, c.n_vars, ROUND(c.pct_clean * 0.3 + 100.0 * c.active_days / NULLIF(c.span_days, 0) * 0.4 + c.n_vars * 10 * 0.3, 2) AS quality_score FROM coverage c JOIN sensors s ON c.sensor_name = s.sensor_name) SELECT sensor_name, broker_name, pct_clean, active_days, span_days, n_vars, quality_score, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY quality_score DESC) AS rank FROM scored ORDER BY rank LIMIT 10;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_24\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Find sensor-days where both average LAeq_1min exceeds 65 dB AND average NO2 exceeds 40 µg/m³ (concurrent noise-pollution events).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH noise_days AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_laeq FROM readings WHERE variable = 'LAeq_1min' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) HAVING AVG(value) > 65), no2_days AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) HAVING AVG(value) > 40) SELECT n.sensor_name, n.day, n.avg_laeq, p.avg_no2 FROM noise_days n JOIN no2_days p ON n.sensor_name = p.sensor_name AND n.day = p.day ORDER BY n.day;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_25\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Long-term NO2 trend: compare first-year mean vs last-year mean per sensor to quantify 10-year air quality change.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH sensor_years AS (SELECT sensor_name, strftime('%Y', timestamp) AS yr, AVG(value) AS mean_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, strftime('%Y', timestamp)), bounds AS (SELECT sensor_name, MIN(yr) AS first_yr, MAX(yr) AS last_yr FROM sensor_years GROUP BY sensor_name) SELECT b.sensor_name, b.first_yr AS first_year, ROUND(f.mean_no2, 3) AS first_yr_mean, b.last_yr AS last_year, ROUND(l.mean_no2, 3) AS last_yr_mean, ROUND(l.mean_no2 - f.mean_no2, 3) AS long_term_delta FROM bounds b JOIN sensor_years f ON b.sensor_name = f.sensor_name AND b.first_yr = f.yr JOIN sensor_years l ON b.sensor_name = l.sensor_name AND b.last_yr = l.yr ORDER BY long_term_delta;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_26\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Weather-pollution interaction: compare average NO2 on wet days (rainfall > 1 mm) vs dry days.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH daily_rainfall AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, SUM(value) AS total_rain_mm FROM readings WHERE variable = 'Rainfall' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)), daily_no2 AS (SELECT sensor_name, DATE(timestamp) AS day, AVG(value) AS avg_no2 FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY sensor_name, DATE(timestamp)) SELECT CASE WHEN r.total_rain_mm > 1 THEN 'Wet day (>1 mm)' ELSE 'Dry day (≤1 mm)' END AS day_type, AVG(n.avg_no2) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n_sensor_days FROM daily_no2 n JOIN daily_rainfall r ON n.sensor_name = r.sensor_name AND n.day = r.day GROUP BY day_type;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_27\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Identify sensors with statistically anomalous flagging rates (exceeding population mean + 2 population standard deviations).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH flag_rates AS (SELECT sensor_name, ROUND(100.0 * SUM(flagged) / COUNT(*), 4) AS pct_flagged FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name), pop_stats AS (SELECT AVG(pct_flagged) AS pop_mean, AVG(pct_flagged*pct_flagged) - AVG(pct_flagged)*AVG(pct_flagged) AS pop_variance FROM flag_rates) SELECT f.sensor_name, f.pct_flagged, s.pop_mean, ROUND(s.pop_mean + 2 * SQRT(s.pop_variance), 4) AS threshold_2sd, ROUND(f.pct_flagged - s.pop_mean, 4) AS excess FROM flag_rates f, pop_stats s WHERE f.pct_flagged > s.pop_mean + 2 * SQRT(s.pop_variance) ORDER BY f.pct_flagged DESC;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_28\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Show the hourly profile of all four core AQ variables (NO2, PM2.5, PM10, O3) simultaneously across the full archive.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH hourly_aq AS (SELECT CAST(strftime('%H', timestamp) AS INTEGER) AS hour, variable, AVG(value) AS avg_val, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings WHERE variable IN ('NO2', 'PM2.5', 'PM10', 'O3') GROUP BY strftime('%H', timestamp), variable) SELECT hour, MAX(CASE WHEN variable = 'NO2'   THEN avg_val END) AS avg_no2, MAX(CASE WHEN variable = 'PM2.5' THEN avg_val END) AS avg_pm25, MAX(CASE WHEN variable = 'PM10'  THEN avg_val END) AS avg_pm10, MAX(CASE WHEN variable = 'O3'    THEN avg_val END) AS avg_o3 FROM hourly_aq GROUP BY hour ORDER BY hour;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_29\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"air_quality\",\n","     \"question\": \"Compute the week-by-week NO2 trend for the full 2013–present archive, including a 5-week rolling average and week-on-week change.\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH weekly AS (SELECT strftime('%Y-%W', timestamp) AS week, AVG(value) AS avg_no2, COUNT(*) AS n FROM readings WHERE variable = 'NO2' GROUP BY strftime('%Y-%W', timestamp)) SELECT week, avg_no2, n, AVG(avg_no2) OVER (ORDER BY week ROWS BETWEEN 4 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS rolling_5week_avg, ROUND(avg_no2 - LAG(avg_no2) OVER (ORDER BY week), 4) AS wow_change FROM weekly ORDER BY week;\"},\n","    {\"id\": \"T5_30\", \"tier\": \"T5\", \"domain\": \"multi_theme\",\n","     \"question\": \"Strategic sensor ranking: score and rank all sensors by data quality (30%), temporal coverage (40%), and thematic breadth (30%).\",\n","     \"sql\": \"WITH base AS (SELECT sensor_name, ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN flagged=0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)/COUNT(*), 2) AS pct_clean, COUNT(DISTINCT DATE(timestamp)) AS active_days, ROUND(JULIANDAY(MAX(timestamp)) - JULIANDAY(MIN(timestamp)), 0) AS span_days, COUNT(DISTINCT variable) AS n_vars FROM readings GROUP BY sensor_name), maxes AS (SELECT MAX(active_days) AS max_active, MAX(n_vars) AS max_vars FROM base), scored AS (SELECT b.sensor_name, s.broker_name, b.pct_clean, b.active_days, b.span_days, b.n_vars, ROUND(b.pct_clean * 0.30 + 100.0 * b.active_days / NULLIF(m.max_active, 0) * 0.40 + 100.0 * b.n_vars / NULLIF(m.max_vars, 0) * 0.30, 2) AS composite_score FROM base b JOIN sensors s ON b.sensor_name = s.sensor_name, maxes m) SELECT sensor_name, broker_name, pct_clean, active_days, span_days, n_vars, composite_score, RANK() OVER (ORDER BY composite_score DESC) AS overall_rank FROM scored ORDER BY overall_rank LIMIT 20;\"},\n","]\n","\n","# ── Summary ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(f\"Total benchmark questions: {len(BENCHMARK_QUESTIONS)}\")\n","for tier in ['T1', 'T2', 'T3', 'T4', 'T5']:\n","    count  = sum(1 for q in BENCHMARK_QUESTIONS if q['tier'] == tier)\n","    domains = set(q['domain'] for q in BENCHMARK_QUESTIONS if q['tier'] == tier)\n","    print(f\"  {tier}: {count} questions | domains: {sorted(domains)}\")\n","\n","# ── Save ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","import os\n","os.makedirs('data_export', exist_ok=True)\n","with open('data_export/benchmark_questions.json', 'w') as f:\n","    json.dump(BENCHMARK_QUESTIONS, f, indent=2)\n","mirror_save(\"benchmark_questions.json\")\n","print(f\"\\nSaved to data_export/benchmark_questions.json\")\n","print(f\"IDs: {[q['id'] for q in BENCHMARK_QUESTIONS[:5]]} … {[q['id'] for q in BENCHMARK_QUESTIONS[-3:]]}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":29,"id":"05343d55","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.550936Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.550285Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-30T04:35:28.07209Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-30T04:35:28.070824Z"},"papermill":{"duration":28.579179,"end_time":"2026-08-30T04:35:28.074651","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-30T04:34:59.495472","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  T1_01: OK (1412 rows)\n","  T1_02: OK (1 rows)\n","  T1_03: OK (27 rows)\n","  T1_04: OK (29 rows)\n","  T1_05: OK (14 rows)\n","  T1_06: OK (1412 rows)\n","  T1_07: OK (709 rows)\n","  T1_08: OK (1 rows)\n","  T1_09: OK (0 rows)\n","  T1_10: OK (1 rows)\n","  T1_11: OK (0 rows)\n","  T1_12: OK (20 rows)\n","  T1_13: OK (0 rows)\n","  T1_14: OK (0 rows)\n","  T1_15: OK (10 rows)\n","  T1_16: OK (2 rows)\n","  T1_17: OK (0 rows)\n","  T1_18: OK (593 rows)\n","  T1_19: OK (0 rows)\n","  T1_20: OK (10 rows)\n","  T1_21: OK (4 rows)\n","  T1_22: OK (0 rows)\n","  T1_23: OK (24 rows)\n","  T1_24: OK (6 rows)\n","  T1_25: OK (1 rows)\n","  T1_26: OK (118 rows)\n","  T1_27: OK (8 rows)\n","  T1_28: OK (1 rows)\n","  T1_29: OK (114 rows)\n","  T1_30: OK (184 rows)\n","  T2_01: OK (23 rows)\n","  T2_02: OK (21 rows)\n","  T2_03: OK (23 rows)\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  T2_04: OK (6 rows)\n","  T2_05: OK (27 rows)\n","  T2_06: OK (52 rows)\n","  T2_07: OK (4 rows)\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["  T2_08: OK (23 rows)\n","  T2_09: OK (14 rows)\n","  T2_10: OK (23 rows)\n